  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oil in the bottom of a large clay or ceramic pot over medium heat.",
    "Add the onion, garlic, and ginger and cook, stirring occasionally, until the onion is softened, about 8 minutes.",
    "Add the lamb and cook, stirring occasionally, until browned on all sides, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the cumin, coriander, cinnamon, turmeric, salt, and pepper, and stir to combine.",
    "Add the prunes and 2 cups of water, and bring to a boil.",
    "Cover the pot and transfer it to the oven.",
    "Bake at 300°F for 2 1/2 hours, or until the lamb is tender.",
    "Stir in the parsley, if using.",
    "Serve the tagine over couscous or rice.",
    "Garnish with additional parsley, if desired."
